{
  "abstract": "A Lean 4 formalization of Murat Can Temeller's October 2026 partial result on Erdős Problem #64 (the Erdős–Gyárfás conjecture): every finite simple graph with minimum degree at least 4 and diameter at most 3 contains a cycle of length 4 or 8, and hence a cycle whose length is a power of 2. Five compared theorems state the result with the diameter hypothesis written as pairwise distances at most 3, as G.ediam ≤ 3, and as G.Connected with G.diam ≤ 3 (Mathlib's G.diam is 0 for a disconnected graph), together with the Erdős–Gyárfás form of the conclusion. The proof follows Temeller's argument: assuming no 4-cycle and no 8-cycle, two vertices share at most one neighbour; if every edge lies in a triangle, triangle detours around a fixed vertex force an 8-cycle, and otherwise an edge in no triangle is analysed through bridges, a funnelling step and the short connections forced by the diameter bound, which close a 4-cycle or an 8-cycle in every case.",
